! vfl_refill_df.strap -- a VFL store's progressive refill raises DF
! (data fetch) only when the refill happens; a DS alarm on the store
! suppresses the whole operation, the refill and its DF with it.
!
! THE RULES, Reference Manual 22-6530-2, read in the page images (PDF =
! printed + 3):
!   printed p.22, Programming Notes: "If an exception condition is
!   detected during the variable field length portion of the operation,
!   the entire operation will be suppressed, and the appropriate
!   indicator will be turned on.  However, if an exception condition is
!   detected during the index modification portion of the operation, only
!   this portion will be suppressed, the variable field length portion
!   having been executed already."
!   printed p.32: "When an address alarm is caused by a data address used
!   in a store-type operation, indicator DS is turned on.  Since this
!   indicator is permanently masked on, storing in core storage is always
!   suppressed, and the operation is always terminated."  "When an address
!   alarm is caused by a data address used in a fetch-type operation,
!   indicator DF is turned on ... If the DF mask bit is zero, the
!   operation proceeds normally."  Addresses Monitored: "All storage
!   addresses actually used by the CPU in the course of an operation are
!   subject to address monitoring.  If an address which is associated with
!   an operation is not actually used, it will not be monitored"; Data
!   Fetch item 3, "The refill address used in index refill operations".
! So when the field's store is protected (DS), the refill -- the index
! modification portion, after the VFL portion -- is not done, its address
! is not used, and DF is NOT turned on even when the refill word is
! protected too.  When the store is not protected the refill is done and a
! protected refill address turns DF on (the DF mask bit is zero here, so
! the operation proceeds).
!
! THE MODEL BUG THIS DECK CLOSES (2026-11-17): the four inline refill
! shapes (ST one word, ST crossing, M+, CM) raised DF up front, before the
! store's DS was known, so a DS-suppressed operation still turned DF on.
! Now DF is raised beside the index hand-back, under the store's !DS guard
! (StretchExecute.bsv, refillDfNote).
!
! SET-UP, vfl_cross_protect's shape: boundaries and the interruption
! address planted DISABLED; lower boundary PW1, upper PEND, control bit 0
! (signal inside), so the area is PW1 and RFP (the protected refill word);
! then BE.  DS's interruption runs entry 19, "BB1, 6.0" (the marker).  The
! DF mask bit (indicator 20) is zero, so DF interrupts nothing.  After each
! case eight NOPs, TI copies the indicators and word 6, BBZ clears the
! marker, SX saves the index register.  Each X is "XW target, 1, RFP":
! count 1, so V+ICR refills.
!
! (D = (16)8000000000000000 is the DS interruption's marker.  The XQ
! words are value = bit address << 40, count << 18, refill: XQ1 =
! (16)0190580000040642, XQ2 = (16)0190680000040642, XQ3 =
! (16)0190480000040642, XQ4 = (16)0190380000040642.)
!   Q1  CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at PW1+.24 through X7: DS.  I1 = 0 (no DF;
!       DS itself is turned off by its interruption), D1 set, X7 = XQ1.
!   Q2  ST(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at PW1+.40 through X6 (one word): DS.  I2 = 0,
!       D2 set, X6 = XQ2.
!   Q3  M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at PW1+.8 through X5: DS.  I3 = 0, D3 set,
!       X5 = XQ3.
!   Q4  ST(V+ICR)(BU,16,8) at PW0+.56 through X4 (crossing into PW1): DS.
!       I4 = 0, D4 set, X4 = XQ4.
!   Q5  CONTROL.  ST(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at UW+.8 through X3: the store is NOT
!       protected, the refill word is.  The store lands, X3 is refilled
!       from RFP, (16)01348000013405DC, and DF is ON: I5 = DF (16)80000000000
!       | XCZ, XVGZ of the pre-refill state (16)9000 | ST's own MOP and RGZ
!       (p.63; the stored 01 is non-zero) (16)120 = (16)80000009120.  (The
!       hand derivation left out ST's MOP and RGZ; the first run showed
!       them, and they are p.63's, as binStoreInd sets them.)  D5 = 0.
! CYCLES is a model pin.
!
! MEASURED INJECTION, 2026-11-17 (in the worktree from a saved copy of the
! final file, restored and compared with cmp; run on this deck and
! vfl_cross_protect, which passes under it):
!   JD the four up-front dfSignal calls put back (the model before this
!      deck): FAIL I1, I2, I3, I4 = (16)80000000000 (DF) ONLY -- each case
!      its own site (CM, ST one word, M+, ST crossing).  Q5 passes.
! Q5 is the control.  CYCLES 1115 (PC 2117); 1119 before the 2026-11-17 preparation floor (measured).
!
        SLC, 1000.0
START   BD,  $+.32
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, PW1
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := PW1
        LVI, $X13, PEND
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := PEND
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit 0: signal INSIDE
        LX,  $X7, XQ1
        LX,  $X6, XQ2
        LX,  $X5, XQ3
        LX,  $X4, XQ4
        LX,  $X3, XQ5
        BE,  $+.32
! ---- Q1: CM with a refill, protected store and refill -------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X7), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        TI, 1, 6, D1
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X7, X7A
! ---- Q2: one-word ST with a refill ---------------------------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X6), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        TI, 1, 6, D2
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X6, X6A
! ---- Q3: M+ with a refill -------------------------------------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X5), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        TI, 1, 6, D3
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X5, X5A
! ---- Q4: crossing ST with a refill ---------------------------------
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        Z, $IND
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,16,8), 0($X4), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        TI, 1, 6, D4
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X4, X4A
! ---- Q5: CONTROL, unprotected store, protected refill ---------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X3), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, $IND, I5
        TI, 1, 6, D5
        BBZ, 6.0, $+1.0
        SX,  $X3, X3A
        Z, $IND
        BD,  $+.32
PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, 1500.0
XQ1     XW, PW1+.24, 1, RFP
XQ2     XW, PW1+.40, 1, RFP
XQ3     XW, PW1+.8, 1, RFP
XQ4     XW, PW0+.56, 1, RFP
XQ5     XW, UW+.8, 1, RFP
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0100000000000000
HBEEF   DD(BU,64), (16)BEEF000000000000
UW      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5

        SLC, 1600.0
PW0     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
PW1     DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
RFP     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0
PEND    DD(BU,64), 0

        SLC, 1700.0
I1      DD(BU,64), 0
I2      DD(BU,64), 0
I3      DD(BU,64), 0
I4      DD(BU,64), 0
I5      DD(BU,64), 0
D1      DD(BU,64), 0
D2      DD(BU,64), 0
D3      DD(BU,64), 0
D4      DD(BU,64), 0
D5      DD(BU,64), 0
X7A     DD(BU,64), 0
X6A     DD(BU,64), 0
X5A     DD(BU,64), 0
X4A     DD(BU,64), 0
X3A     DD(BU,64), 0

        SLC, 1800.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, 1819.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
